flycast: include <unistd.h> outside Apple for getpid()

The bundled libzip's mkstemp.c calls getpid() unconditionally, but only pulls
in <unistd.h> under "#ifdef __APPLE__".  Every other POSIX target got the
declaration by luck through another header; gcc 14 no longer allows the
implicit declaration and the build stops:

  core/deps/libzip/mkstemp.c:70:15: error: implicit declaration of function
                                   'getpid' [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

Widen the guard to "#ifndef _WIN32", which is where <unistd.h> genuinely does
not exist.  Apple keeps the include it already had.

Build-enablement only -- no behaviour change.

--- a/core/deps/libzip/mkstemp.c
+++ b/core/deps/libzip/mkstemp.c
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
-#ifdef __APPLE__
+#ifndef _WIN32
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 
